<title>UK: TENNIS-WIMBLEDON MEN'S DOUBLES RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-WIMBLEDON MEN'S DOUBLES RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Men's doubles first round results</p>
<p>at Wimbledon on Sunday:</p>
<p>Sander Groen (Netherlands)/Sasa Hirszon (Croatia) beat Wayne</p>
<p>Arthurs (Australia)/Andrew Kratzmann (Australia) 7-6 (7-5) 6-4</p>
<p>Cristian Brandi (Italy)/Filippo Messori (Italy) beat Mahesh</p>
<p>Bhupathi (India)/Leander Paes (India) 6-4 3-6 6-3</p>
<p>Trevor Kronemann (U.S.)/David MacPherson (Australia) beat Robbie</p>
<p>Koenig (South Africa)/Andrew Rueb (U.S.) 6-1 6-4</p>
<p>Dave Randall (U.S.)/Jack Waite (U.S.) beat 16-Joshua Eagle</p>
<p>(Australia)/Andrew Florent (Australia) 7-6 (7-5) 6-2</p>
<p>6-Ellis Ferreira (South Africa)/Patrick Galbraith (U.S.) beat</p>
<p>T.J. Middleton (U.S.)/Chris Woodruff (U.S.) 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>15-Grant Connell (Canada)/Scott Davis (U.S.) beat Peter Nyborg</p>
<p>(Sweden)/Daniel Orsanic (Argentina) 7-5 5-7 6-3</p>
<p>Henrik Holm (Sweden)/Nils Holm (Sweden) beat Martin Lee</p>
<p>(Britain)/James Trotman (Britain) 6-4 3-6 6-3</p>
<p>13-Martin Damm (Czech Republic)/Pavel Vizner (Czech Republic)</p>
<p>beat David Adams (South Africa)/Marius Barnard (South Africa)</p>
<p>7-6 (7-4)</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>4-Mark Knowles (Bahamas)/Daniel Nestor (Canada) beat Tom Kempers</p>
<p>(Netherlands)/Menno Oosting (Netherlands) 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>John-Laffnie De Jager (South Africa)/Tom Nijssen (Netherlands)</p>
<p>beat Danny Sapsford (Britain)/Chris Wilkinson (Britain) 7-6</p>
<p>(7-4) 6-4</p>
<p>Pablo Albano (Argentina)/Slava Dosedel (Czech Republic) beat</p>
<p>Joao Cunha-Silva (Portugal)/Nuno Marques (Portugal) 6-7 (5-7)</p>
<p>6-3 7-5</p>
<p>Bill Behrens (U.S.)/Chris Haggard (South Africa) beat 14-Libor</p>
<p>Pimek (Belgium)/Byron Talbot (South Africa) 4-6 6-3 14-12</p>
<p>11-Neil Broad (Britain)/Piet Norval (South Africa) beat Ben</p>
<p>Ellwood (Australia)/Peter Tramacchi (Australia) 6-4 5-7 9-7</p>
<p>Marcos Ondruska (South Africa)/Grant Stafford (South Africa)</p>
<p>beat Max Mirnyi (Belarus)/Kevin Ullyett (South Africa) 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>Wayne Black (Zimbabwe)/Jim Grabb (U.S.) beat Regis Lavergne</p>
<p>(France)/Stephane Simian (France) 6-1 6-4</p>
<p>9-Jonas Bjorkman (Sweden)/Nicklas Kulti (Sweden) beat Jan</p>
<p>Siemerink (Netherlands)/Jason Stoltenberg (Australia) 7-6 (8-6)</p>
<p>6-3</p>
<p>Emilio Sanchez (Spain)/Fabrice Santoro (France) beat</p>
<p>3-Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia)/Daniel Vacek (Czech Republic) 6-2</p>
<p>7-6 (7-5)</p>
<p>Jens Knippschild (Germany)/Jeff Tarango (U.S.) beat Rikard</p>
<p>Bergh (Sweden)/David Ekerot (Sweden) 6-4 7-5</p>
<p>8-Rick Leach (U.S.)/Jonathan Stark (U.S.) beat Jean-Philippe</p>
<p>Fleurian (France)/Guy Forget (France) 6-4 6-3</p>
<p>Stephen Noteboom (Netherlands)/Fernon Wibier (Netherlands) beat</p>
<p>5-Sebastien Lareau (Canada)/Alex O'Brien (U.S.) 7-6 (7-5) 3-6</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>Byron Black (Zimbabwe)/Justin Gimelstob (U.S.) beat Kelly Jones</p>
<p>(U.S.)/Scott Melville (U.S.) 6-4 5-7 6-2</p>
<p>Kent Kinnear (U.S.)/Aleksandar Kitinov (Macedonia) beat Patrick</p>
<p>Baur (Germany)/Marc Goellner (Germany) 7-6 (7-5) 6-7 (6-8) 14-12</p>
